{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1793596129688475596,"compiled_state":{"alias":"daemonic-entodermal-tuatara","assignee":null,"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":2,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"11ff52b3a606ed0769611899a417cbb692d79939a4c20c6995c544d1b9e1fbd0","event_uuid":"d28d13e4-8df0-45a7-afee-630b7e1c332b","position":{"commit_sha":"fe0555324a0bf2b6718e042d5bc98652a28ab3fc","position":"1793590806708361544-d28d13e4-8df0-45a7-afee-630b7e1c332b"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"0fb3c9a288704b98b90edfcffc5280de07d24fe65dec7fb312002b80a52eeafd","event_uuid":"ecf97643-5664-4578-960f-43d720c1fcb7","position":{"commit_sha":"0e1c21019c2fee2a9fcc294f8abe3bef3a34c284","position":"1793590821677233830-ecf97643-5664-4578-960f-43d720c1fcb7"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1793590806708361544,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"ecf97643-5664-4578-960f-43d720c1fcb7","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"47c8-97ac-eff3-4e88"}],"description":"## Problem\n\n`src/rebar/similar/index.py` recovers from a corrupt or version-stale index by calling\n`_discard(path)` — which unlinks the database file and its `-wal`/`-shm` sidecars — and then\nrebuilding via `_open_one`. That path carries **no lock**.\n\nEvery other write in the subsystem serializes on sqlite's own write lock: `catchup.py` opens\nits transaction with `BEGIN IMMEDIATE` under a `busy_timeout`, and `catchup.py`'s module\ndocstring states \"Concurrent reconcilers serialize on sqlite's write lock.\" The\ndiscard-and-rebuild path is an unlocked twin of that write path — `os.unlink` is not covered\nby a sqlite lock, and there is no flock or `threading.Lock` anywhere under `src/rebar/similar`.\n\n## Why two executors can reach it at once\n\n`open_index` is called independently by each MCP request handler on the create path\n(`src/rebar/_mcp_serving.py` serves concurrent handlers on a worker thread). `_open_one`\nraises `StaleIndex`/`sqlite3.DatabaseError` for **both** callers before either has finished\nrebuilding, so both enter the recovery branch.\n\n## Harm\n\nTwo interleavings, both silent:\n\n1. Executor B's `os.unlink(path + \"-wal\")` removes the WAL sidecar of executor A's live\n   connection, leaving A's FTS5 state inconsistent.\n2. Executor A commits its catch-up rows into an inode that B's later unlink has detached. The\n   on-disk index then silently loses those rows and serves empty results until the next full\n   rebuild.\n\nBoth produce exactly the failure mode ADR 0122's design set out to avoid: a silently frozen\nindex is indistinguishable from a healthy index that matched nothing.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] The discard-and-rebuild path in `src/rebar/similar/index.py` is serialized against\n      itself, so two concurrent callers that both observe a corrupt or stale index produce\n      one rebuild rather than two interleaved ones.\n- [ ] A test starts two threads that both hit the recovery branch on the same index path\n      (barrier-synchronized, as `test_concurrent_catch_up_runs_leave_a_sound_index_holding_both_tickets`\n      already does for the normal write path) and asserts afterwards that\n      `PRAGMA integrity_check` returns `ok` and that every ticket written before the\n      corruption is still retrievable.\n- [ ] That test fails against the current unsynchronized implementation.\n- [ ] If the chosen fix adds a lock, it carries a `# mechanism-ok: lock <name> — <reason>`\n      marker at its definition site, since the mechanism-delta ratchet fails on any\n      unadmitted new mechanism.\n- [ ] `make verify` passes.\n\n## Provenance\n\nFound by `rebar review-code` as an advisory finding on ticket `47c8-97ac-eff3-4e88`'s change\n(Change-Id `I3e1c9d8fa0c95a152b9be91ed8357a6ad2389e73`). Three sibling advisories from the same\nreview — a `limit <= 0` off-by-one, an `UNKNOWN_MTIME` sentinel compared by equality, and an\ninaccurate warm-path docstring — were fixed inside 47c8 itself. This one is deferred because\nit is a design change to the recovery path rather than a localized correction, and because the\nrace predates the reviewed change in shape: it is a property of the recovery branch, not of\nthe new indexing code.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["complexity-reduction","similar-tickets"],"ticket_id":"4932-ea62-cf4f-451b","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Serialize the similar-index discard-and-rebuild path","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["d28d13e4-8df0-45a7-afee-630b7e1c332b","ecf97643-5664-4578-960f-43d720c1fcb7"]},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1793596129688475596,"uuid":"cf15f000-61cb-4dbc-9110-7d56df2a2723"}